## §5 Tier system

Static buff/debuff infrastructure for `soak` and `hit_chance`. Lives
in `pod_combat_tier_effects.txt`.

### Data model

| Var | Role |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_{side,c{N}}_base_soak` | soak before any tier effects |
| `pod_combat_{side,c{N}}_base_hit_chance` | hit chance before any tier effects |
| `pod_combat_{side,c{N}}_soak` | live soak (base + buff mags - debuff mags) |
| `pod_combat_{side,c{N}}_hit_chance` | live hit chance (same formula) |
| `pod_combat_{side,c{N}}_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier` | current tier (1/2/3) |

### Magnitudes

| Tier | Magnitude |
|---:|---|
| 1 (small) | ±10 |
| 2 (medium) | ±20 |
| 3 (large) | ±30 |

### Apply / revert flow (recalc-from-base, no deltas)

- **Applying tier N:** set the tier var, then call a recalc effect.
  The stat is rebuilt from base + sum of active tier magnitudes,
  clamped on write. Clamping losses do NOT accumulate because each
  apply and each revert starts from the pristine base.
- **Round end:** round-duration tier vars are cleared, then every
  slot is recalculated. Combat-duration tiers persist.
- **Combat end:** all tier vars cleared.

### When to edit `pod_combat_tier_effects.txt` directly

- The number of slots changes (currently 10).
- The tier stat categories change (currently `soak`, `hit`).
- Tier magnitudes change (must remain in lockstep with the move-side
  tier setters in `pod_combat_move_init_effects.txt`).

